+# Milestone 2 — S-6 Mutation Testing Summary
+
+**Story:** S-6 scheduled monthly dues payment (AC-19 to AC-22)
+**Tool:** mutmut 3.8.1 (Python 3.12.3, pytest 9.2.0, Hypothesis 6.170.15)
+**Prepared by:** Claude Code (AGENT-22, Prompt 88) from the evidence files named below, for human review.
+
+This summary is not tool output. Every result below is copied from a raw evidence file or from a
+check the human operator reported. Each item is marked:
+
+- **[Verified]**: recorded in a raw evidence file named in the item.
+- **[Reported]**: run and reported by the human operator; no raw evidence file holds the output.
+- **[Inferred]**: concluded from reading source code or tool source; not observed in a run.
+- **[Open]**: a design question that needs a human decision.
+
+## 1. Objective and scope
+
+The experiment asked whether the S-6 tests detect deliberate faults in the payment logic. It also
+asked whether the two Hypothesis properties (`tests/test_s6_properties.py`) detect faults that the
+regression and acceptance tests miss.
+
+mutmut generated 603 mutants for `app/payments.py` and `app/db.py`. **Only 30 selected mutants were
+executed.** Every score in this document refers to those 30 mutants, not to all 603.
+
+## 2. Source files under mutation
+
+`pyproject.toml` (configuration commit `9474ad4`):
+
+```toml
+[tool.mutmut]
+source_paths = ["app"]
+only_mutate = ["app/payments.py", "app/db.py"]
+also_copy = ["pytest.ini"]
+pytest_add_cli_args_test_selection = [
+    "tests/test_s6_payments.py",
+    "tests/acceptance",
+]
+```
+
+Of `app/db.py`, only `_retry_allowed` mutants were selected. It runs no SQL, so no selected mutant
+changed a database connection, schema or query.
+
+## 3. Selected mutants
+
+30 mutants from four functions. The nine pilot mutants are included.
+
+| Function | Selected mutants |
+|---|---|
+| `app.payments._count_outcome` | `_1`, `_2`, `_3`, `_5`, `_19`, `_20` |
+| `app.payments.run_due_payments` | `_1`, `_2`, `_3`, `_9`, `_69`, `_78`, `_89`, `_97`, `_109`, `_114`, `_128`, `_146`, `_174` |
+| `app.payments._charge_pending` | `_4`, `_29`, `_36`, `_38` |
+| `app.db._retry_allowed` | `_1`, `_2`, `_3`, `_17`, `_22`, `_24`, `_29` |
+
+The selection covers outcome counting, the guard against paying a month twice (idempotency), due-date
+boundaries, attempt numbering and limits, retry timing, and the handling of processor results. The
+exact diffs are in `evidence/mutation-selected-diffs.txt` **[Verified]**.
+
+Pilot: 9 of 9 pilot mutants were killed (`evidence/mutation-pilot.txt`,
+`evidence/mutation-pilot-extended.txt`) **[Verified]**.
+
+## 4. Test selections
+
+| Run | Tests selected | Source of this information |
+|---|---|---|
+| Baseline A | `tests/test_s6_payments.py`, `tests/acceptance` | config printed in `evidence/mutation-baseline.txt` **[Verified]** |
+| Baseline B | Baseline A plus `tests/test_s6_properties.py` | config printed in `evidence/mutation-properties.txt`, line 11 **[Verified]** |
+| After the regression tests | `tests/test_s6_payments.py`, `tests/acceptance`, now including the three new tests | `evidence/mutation-after.txt` does not print the config. The committed `pyproject.toml` has the Baseline A selection **[Inferred]** |
+
+## 5–6. Baseline A and Baseline B
+
+| Run | Killed | Survived | Timeout or other | Score |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| A: regression and acceptance tests | 25 | 5 | 0 | 83.33% |
+| B: A plus Hypothesis properties | 25 | 5 | 0 | 83.33% |
+
+**[Verified]** in `evidence/mutation-baseline.txt` and `evidence/mutation-properties.txt`. The same five
+mutants survived both runs:
+
+- `app.payments.x__count_outcome__mutmut_5`
+- `app.payments.x__count_outcome__mutmut_20`
+- `app.payments.x_run_due_payments__mutmut_89`
+- `app.payments.x_run_due_payments__mutmut_109`
+- `app.payments.x__charge_pending__mutmut_38`
+
+**Why the Hypothesis properties added no kills:**
+
+- `mutmut tests-for-mutant` confirmed that Property 1 was selected for `_count_outcome__mutmut_5`
+  **[Reported]**. mutmut's stats file lists the property under `app.payments.x__count_outcome`
+  (`mutants/mutmut-stats.json`) **[Verified]**.
+- A verbose Hypothesis run showed that all 10 Property 1 examples used a single resident
+  **[Reported]**. Property 1 can only kill `_5` with an example that schedules both residents and runs
+  on or after the due day.
+- Property 1 checks only `charged`, never `skipped`. Its processor is always available, and all units
+  share one due day. Property 2 uses one unit and checks only the payment history and the processor
+  calls **[Inferred]**.
+
+## 7. Three deterministic regression tests
+
+Added to `tests/test_s6_payments.py` (`agent-patches/AGENT-21-M2-mutation-killing-tests.patch`):
+
+| Test | Requirement | Expected result | Target mutant |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `test_d16_two_units_charged_in_one_run_are_both_counted` | D16, R4 | `RunResult(charged=2, failed=0, skipped=0)`; both units Paid; two processor calls | `x__count_outcome__mutmut_5` (`charged = 1`) |
+| `test_d16_two_unavailable_charges_are_both_counted_as_skipped` | D16, R4 | `RunResult(charged=0, failed=0, skipped=2)`; both units Pending | `x__count_outcome__mutmut_20` (`skipped = 1`) |
+| `test_r4_paid_unit_does_not_stop_the_run_for_a_later_unit` | R4, D25, D27 | `due_schedules()` reaches MR-12 first; `RunResult(charged=1, failed=0, skipped=1)`; MR-12 has a manual Paid payment; MR-20 has an attempt-1 debit Paid payment; only MR-20 is charged | `x_run_due_payments__mutmut_89` (Paid `continue` becomes `break`) |
+
+The focused run gave 3 passed, 102 deselected **[Reported]**.
+
+## 8. After the regression tests
+
+| Run | Killed | Survived | Timeout or other | Score |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|
+| After the regression tests | 28 | 2 | 0 | 93.33% |
+
+**[Verified]** in `evidence/mutation-after.txt`. Its "Mutant results" list shows 28 killed and 2
+survived, and the run ended with `MUTMUT_RUN_EXIT_STATUS=0`. `_5`, `_20` and `_89` are now killed.
+`_109` and `_38` survived.
+
+## 9. Comparison
+
+| Mutant | A | B | After |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| `x__count_outcome__mutmut_5` | survived | survived | **killed** |
+| `x__count_outcome__mutmut_20` | survived | survived | **killed** |
+| `x_run_due_payments__mutmut_89` | survived | survived | **killed** |
+| `x_run_due_payments__mutmut_109` | survived | survived | survived |
+| `x__charge_pending__mutmut_38` | survived | survived | survived |
+| the other 25 | killed | killed | killed |
+| **Score (30 selected mutants)** | **83.33%** | **83.33%** | **93.33%** |
+
+The score rose by 10 percentage points. The rise came from the deterministic regression tests, not
+from the Hypothesis properties.
+
+## 10. The two remaining survivors
+
+### `app.payments.x_run_due_payments__mutmut_109`
+
+The mutation is `prior["attempt"] < settings.MAX_PAYMENT_ATTEMPTS` becoming `<=`
+(`app/payments.py:100`).
+
+**Classification:** survived. It can be observed under concurrency, and the expected value is an
+unresolved design question **[Open]**. It is not equivalent in every case.
+
+- **Sequential runs [Inferred]:** the mutant claims an attempt beyond the maximum. The locked re-check
+  in `db._retry_allowed` refuses it (`attempt > max_attempts`, `app/db.py:197`), so the run continues
+  and counts nothing, as the original does.
+- **A concurrent manual payment [Inferred]:** suppose a manual payment commits between the Paid
+  pre-check (`app/payments.py:93`) and the claim for a schedule whose attempts are used up. The
+  mutant's claim then returns `"Paid"`, and the run adds 1 to `RunResult.skipped`
+  (`app/payments.py:112-113`). The original continues without counting. The same single-process
+  monkeypatch technique as `test_ac22_manual_payment_racing_retry_creation_prevents_charge`
+  (`tests/test_s6_payments.py:926`) could show this.
+- **Design question [Open]:** If a schedule has used up its automatic payment attempts and a manual
+  payment arrives between the Paid pre-check and the claim, should `RunResult.skipped` increase by one
+  or stay unchanged? D35 ("exhausted schedules are not counted in RunResult") supports *unchanged*.
+  D25's Paid-first check and D16's definition of `skipped` support *increase*. No test was added,
+  because neither value is specified.
+
+### `app.payments.x__charge_pending__mutmut_38`
+
+The mutation is `return "Unchanged"` becoming `return "XXUnchangedXX"` (`app/payments.py:54`).
+
+**Classification:** equivalent through the reviewed public API (`run_due_payments`, `RunResult`,
+payment history). It is not identical when the private function is called directly **[Inferred]**.
+
+- `_count_outcome` counts only `"Paid"`, `"Failed"` and `None` (`app/payments.py:63-68`), so both
+  markers are ignored.
+- `test_f11_agreeing_completion_is_left_unchanged_and_not_counted` (`tests/test_s6_payments.py:1112`)
+  asserts `RunResult()`, which holds for both markers.
+- A direct call to `_charge_pending` would return a different string. No test calls it, and none was
+  added to pin a private marker.
+
+## 11. Coverage and regression testing
+
+`python -m pytest --cov=app --cov-branch --cov-report=term-missing --cov-fail-under=80`:
+202 collected, 202 passed, 1 warning, 487.74 s. Total: 425 statements, 18 missed, 140 branches,
+12 partial. Coverage: **94.34%**, above the 80% threshold. **[Verified]** in
+`evidence/mutation-regression-tests.txt`.
+
+The warning is the existing `StarletteDeprecationWarning` about `httpx` with `starlette.testclient`.
+It does not fail any test.
+
+**Coverage versus mutation score:** branch coverage was 94.34% both before and after the three new
+tests. Over the same period the mutation score on the 30 selected mutants rose from 83.33% to
+93.33%. The lines of `_5`, `_20` and `_89` were already covered; they survived because no assertion
+distinguished their behavior.
+
+## 12. Protected-file verification
+
+```bash
+git diff --exit-code m2-tests-locked -- tests/acceptance tests/conftest.py tests/__init__.py conftest.py pytest.ini
+```
+
+The result was `PROTECTED-UNCHANGED` **[Reported]**.
+
+## 13. Database cleanup
+
+```bash
+psql "$COMMUNITYCONNECT_TEST_DATABASE_URL" -Atc "SELECT current_database(), (SELECT count(*) FROM pg_namespace WHERE nspname LIKE 'test_%')"
+```
+
+The result was `communityconnect_test|0`: no test schemas were left behind **[Reported]**.
+
+## 14. Reproducibility notes
+
+- All runs used one worker (`--max-children 1`) and named the 30 mutants explicitly.
+- **Cache warning [Verified]:** `evidence/mutation-after.txt` reports `0 files mutated, 8 ignored,
+  2 unmodified`. It also warns that 7 non-Python files had changed since the last full run and that
+  "cached results were kept". The after-run therefore reused the existing `mutants/` workspace:
+  mutants were not regenerated, and the 603 mutants were not freshly re-run.
+- **[Inferred]** mutmut 3.8.1 re-runs mutants that are named on the command line even when a result
+  is cached (`mutmut/__main__.py`, `_run`). The after-run's stats phase also ran again. The 30 named
+  mutants were therefore re-executed against the updated tests. The application source was unchanged
+  (`2 unmodified`), so the mutant code was the same as in A and B.
+- `evidence/mutation-after.txt` does not record the test-selection configuration (see section 4).
+- To reproduce from scratch: delete `mutants/`, then run the same 30 names with `--max-children 1`.
+
+## 15. Limitations and open questions
+
+1. The scores cover 30 selected mutants out of 603 generated, from four functions. They are not a
+   mutation score for the whole of `app/payments.py` or `app/db.py`.
+2. `_109`: the design question in section 10 needs a human decision **[Open]**.
+3. `_38`: equivalent only through the public API **[Inferred]**.
+4. The after-run used a cached workspace and does not print its configuration (section 14).
+5. The protected-file check, the database cleanup, the focused three-test run, the verbose Hypothesis
+   run and the `tests-for-mutant` check were reported by the human operator. Their output is not in
+   an evidence file.
+6. The race behavior of `_109` was analyzed by reading code only. No test has run it.
